   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to an\nexemption for certain property from the prohibition of alcohol sales within a\ncertain distance from a place of worship",
    "basePrintNo": "S6891",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6891-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §64, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6891\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to an\nexemption for certain property from the prohibition of alcohol sales\nwithin a certain distance from a place of worship\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill will allow Nettie's Restaurant in Queens, NY to sell alcoholic\nbeverages\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAdds paragraph e-15 to the alcoholic beverage control law to grant a\nliquor licenses to Nettie's Restaurant in Queens, NY, which is currently\nwithin 200 ft. of a place of worship, thus barring it from alcohol sales\nper NYS alcoholic beverage control law\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNettie's Restaurant has been going strong for a number of years absent\nthe sale of alcoholic beverages. This bill will allow them to sell alco-\nhol. The church that is within 200 feet of the establishment has submit-\nted a letter to the State Liquor Authority stating they would be grate-\nful if the state granted such license to Nettie's. In light of their\nstatement and the continued good nature of the Nettie's business in the\ncommunity, they require a legislative bill to authorize liquor sales.\nThis bill will enable them to do that.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis law will take effect immediately.\n",
